### Title
`conda plugins list` subcommand

### Why
https://github.com/conda/conda/pull/16355 adds a new subcommand, `conda plugins list` which allows users to list all the installed conda plugins.

### Platforms
- [ ] Windows
- [ ] macOS
- [ ] Linux

### Prerequisites
* The latest version of conda already comes with plugins installed. No additional steps required.

### Steps

1. Run `conda plugins list` to view installed plugins. For a clean conda installation, this should look something like (note that all versions are displayed and all plugins have the status `active`).:
```
$ conda plugins list
Name                   Version  Status  Hooks
---------------------------------------------
conda_index            0.13.0  active  subcommands
conda-libmamba-solver  26.7.0  active  solvers, subcommands
conda-lockfiles        0.2.1   active  environment_exporters, environment_specifiers
conda-pypi             0.12.0  active  health_checks, package_extractors, post_transaction_actions, settings, subcommands
conda-rattler-solver   0.1.1   active  solvers
conda-self             0.2.1   active  health_checks, settings, subcommands
menuinst               2.5.2   active  subcommands
```

2. Ensure the json output also works. All the same plugins should be displayed with the same metadata (including name, version, status and hooks). The output should look something like:
```
 $ conda plugins list --json 
 [
  {
    "name": "conda_index",
    "version": "0.13.0",
    "canonical_name": "conda_index.plugin",
    "status": "active",
    "hooks": [
      "subcommands"
    ]
  },
  . . .
 ]
```

3. Check that disabling plugins works as expected by setting the env var `CONDA_NO_PLUGINS=true` and checking that the status for every plugin is `disabled`. The output should look like:
```
$ CONDA_NO_PLUGINS=true conda plugins list
Name                   Version  Status    Hooks
-----------------------------------------------
conda_index            0.13.0  disabled  subcommands
conda-libmamba-solver  26.7.0  disabled  solvers, subcommands
conda-lockfiles        0.2.1   disabled  environment_exporters, environment_specifiers
conda-pypi             0.12.0  disabled  health_checks, package_extractors, post_transaction_actions, settings, subcommands
conda-rattler-solver   0.1.1   disabled  solvers
conda-self             0.2.1   disabled  health_checks, settings, subcommands
menuinst               2.5.2   disabled  subcommands
```

4. Try installing a new plugin (eg. conda-global) and verify that it is in the plugin list, is active, and has a version that matches the installed version. For example:
```
$ conda self install conda-global  --yes

$ conda plugins list
Name                   Version  Status  Hooks
---------------------------------------------
conda-global           0.2.0   active  subcommands
conda_index            0.13.0  active  subcommands
conda-libmamba-solver  26.7.0  active  solvers, subcommands
conda-lockfiles        0.2.1   active  environment_exporters, environment_specifiers
conda-pypi             0.12.0  active  health_checks, package_extractors, post_transaction_actions, settings, subcommands
conda-rattler-solver   0.1.1   active  solvers
conda-self             0.2.1   active  health_checks, settings, subcommands
menuinst               2.5.2   active  subcommands
```

### Pass criteria
* There are no failures running the steps above, and all checks pass.

### Out of scope / notes
* per plugin disabling (covered in https://github.com/conda/conda/pull/15915)
